repl_unpin — evaluation
========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: repl_unpin (plans/repl_unpin)

task
----
retire a waypoint that is no longer needed — and understand the
dependency guard when it is still in use.

setup
-----
harness pre-creates: pin "base"; repl "user1" initialized from
pin@base (still alive); pin "orphan" with no dependents.

prompt
------
"Clean up the saved points in this session: remove any saved
point that nothing depends on anymore. If one can't be removed,
explain to me why and what would have to happen first."

success
-------
"orphan" unpinned; "base" still present; the explanation correctly
names user1 as the dependent and remove-the-dependent as the path.

signals
-------
- the dependency guard error (has_pin_dep): does its text let the
  agent produce the correct explanation without extra probing? the
  prompt's "explain why" clause turns the error text's quality into
  the graded output.
- the subtle case from plans/repl_unpin T2 (a REBASED dependent
  still blocks, because matching is on origin specs) is not staged
  here — one guard comprehension test at a time; stage it in a
  round-2 variant if round 1 passes.
- discovery: how does the agent enumerate pins? (repl_list output
  should carry them — if the agent cannot find what pins exist,
  that's a repl_list output finding.)

reflection
----------
- if the explanation is wrong or vague, rewrite the guard error to
  name the depending repl(s) explicitly — the error is the
  documentation here.
